SigV4 test vectors
==================

The directories under v4/ are copied, unmodified, from the AWS Common Runtime
authentication library:

  Source:   https://github.com/awslabs/aws-c-auth
  Path:     tests/aws-signing-test-suite/v4
  Commit:   3d29adcecf5c032131acee9f4125a636d2aaea6a
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0 (the LICENSE file next to this NOTICE is the
            repository's own, copied from the same commit)
  Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.

Per case we vendor request.txt, context.json, header-canonical-request.txt,
header-string-to-sign.txt and header-signature.txt. They were fetched with
`go run ./internal/fetchvectors` and are used by TestAWSSigningTestSuite,
which checks every case at the canonical-request, string-to-sign and
signature levels.

Not vendored, and why
---------------------

  * the sibling suite v4a/ -- SigV4a (asymmetric, multi-region) is a different
    algorithm and is out of scope;
  * the query-* files of each case (presigned URLs, signature in the query
    string) and the *-signed-request.txt files -- this library signs with the
    Authorization header only;
  * S3-specific cases -- the v4 directory of this commit contains none.

All 38 cases of v4/ are run. The suite's request path is the raw text of the
request line; the test hands it to the signer as the URL's Opaque form, which
the signer takes as the wire path.
